{"name":"Brunette","hex":"#664238","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Brunette","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from French."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Brunette"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brunette (singer)","blocks":[{"text":"Elen Yeremyan, known professionally as Brunette, is an Armenian singer-songwriter. She represented Armenia in the Eurovision Song Contest 2023 with the song \"Future Lover\", finishing in 14th place."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Brunette_at_Eurovision_Turquoise_Carpet_2023_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Brunette_at_Eurovision_Turquoise_Carpet_2023_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brunette_(singer)"},{"title":"Brunette (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Brunette\" is a song by American country music singer Tucker Wetmore. It was released on January 12, 2026 as the fourth single from his debut studio album, What Not To (2025). It was written by Chris LaCorte, Chase McGill, Josh Miller and Blake Pendergrass."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/15/Tucker_Wetmore_-_Brunette_LP_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brunette_(song)"},{"title":"Brown hair","blocks":[{"text":"Brown hair, also referred to as brunette, is the second-most common human hair color, after black hair. It varies from light to dark brown. It is characterized by moderate levels of the dark pigment eumelanin and low levels of the pale pigment pheomelanin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Woman_with_long_brown_hair%2C_close-up_view.jpg/330px-Woman_with_long_brown_hair%2C_close-up_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_hair"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org